{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"body":"Claim strength and source representations distinguished explicitly.\n\nInspected: Read complete source, syntactic homogeneity constraints, actual circuit evaluation, IMM matrix product and upperGateBound; compared three separate paper assertions.","content_sha256":"sha256:c8fefad9d9c207e4285d616703f43b78dae03f2cdd7fa658f815cea1f3212b17","fingerprint":"sha256:bd837c797b4a51eba6c96eb434dac925b1055130122d506c7096fa0201530ae7","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Claim strength and source representations distinguished explicitly.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:f9c478730e4609f5ae2ad51ffac1e21f55c1391f41290664af7fe9eb4e7c1196","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.Problem335.main"],"explanation":"The first conjunct states that every sufficiently large syntactically homogeneous depth-five complex circuit computing IMM has at least n^(sqrt(n)/400) gates. This is the paper headline with its stated explicit constant, using the inspected layer-by-layer polynomial evaluation and gate count.","fingerprint":"sha256:1e718087f263196f5653b091c59878e7fd78bfae3b22308839ee70ef5998b744","limitations":"This paper link covers the complex-field lower-bound conjunct, not the other two clauses.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Homogeneous-depth-five-lower-bounds-for-iterated-matrix-multiplication-September-25-2026#thm:main","statement_sha256":"sha256:f74187a0ea6c2b9372758fdd901d33b09497580378e1bb0c79183b4f9659477c"},{"declarations":["OAI.Problem335.main"],"explanation":"The second conjunct gives one eventual threshold uniformly over characteristic-zero fields and the same n^(sqrt(n)/400) gate lower bound. That is the characteristic-zero extension, with no bottom fan-in restriction in the circuit structure.","fingerprint":"sha256:8bd77ccdf4ba5928eb74e3f8c936cf9ca1c2821a842d2d76097e1b64d6855f54","limitations":"Only the second conjunct is attached to this corollary.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Homogeneous-depth-five-lower-bounds-for-iterated-matrix-multiplication-September-25-2026#cor:characteristic-zero","statement_sha256":"sha256:cf285f5010b2c769af94b181f447270f498976c4712cb15279201318f5ed649e"},{"declarations":["OAI.Problem335.main"],"explanation":"The third conjunct constructs circuits over any field for n≥2 with gate bound 2n³+rn²+rn^(t+1)+n^(r−1)+1 and upper estimate n^(sqrt(n)+4). The definitions t=ceil(sqrt(n)) and r=ceil(n/t) agree with the constructive upper-bound proposition.","fingerprint":"sha256:09f49941f70e80d046423373d36553a11bbcbc8a804a19088faa02cd72145a66","limitations":"The upper-bound conjunct is separate from the lower-bound claims.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Homogeneous-depth-five-lower-bounds-for-iterated-matrix-multiplication-September-25-2026#prop:upper","statement_sha256":"sha256:b8be8e29c310aed3c23b49cc611a82477adf1e077f36ea6f164183ad863d78b8"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/DepthFive.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Homogeneous-depth-five-lower-bounds-for-iterated-matrix-multiplication-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L53","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Homogeneous-depth-five-lower-bounds-for-iterated-matrix-multiplication-September-25-